# Phoenix Implementations

This directory contains the implementations for the Phoenix signature algorithm instances.

## Directory Structure

```
Implementations/
├── README                           # This file
├── Reference_Implementation/        # Reference implementation (ISO C, platform-independent)
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-128f/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-128f instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-128s/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-128s instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-192f/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-192f instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-192s/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-192s instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-256f/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-256f instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-256s/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-256s instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-384f/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-384f instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-384s/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-384s instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-512f/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-512f instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SHAKE-512s/          # Phoenix-SHAKE-512s instance
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-128f/            # Phoenix-SM3-128f instance (symlink)
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-128s/            # Phoenix-SM3-128s instance (symlink)
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-192f/            # Phoenix-SM3-192f instance (symlink)
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-192s/            # Phoenix-SM3-192s instance (symlink)
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-256f/            # Phoenix-SM3-256f instance (symlink)
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-256s/            # Phoenix-SM3-256s instance (symlink)
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-384f/            # Phoenix-SM3-384f instance (symlink)
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-384s/            # Phoenix-SM3-384s instance (symlink)
│   ├── Phoenix-SM3-512f/            # Phoenix-SM3-512f instance (symlink)
│   └── Phoenix-SM3-512s/            # Phoenix-SM3-512s instance (symlink)
├── Optimized_Implementation/        # Optimized implementation (64-bit PC processor)
└── Additional_Implementation/       # Additional implementations (e.g., 32-bit embedded)
```

## Algorithm Instances

### SHAKE-based Instances

| Instance | Security Level | Variant |
|----------|---------------|---------|
| Phoenix-SHAKE-128f | 128-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-128s | 128-bit | Small |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-192f | 192-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-192s | 192-bit | Small |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-256f | 256-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-256s | 256-bit | Small |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-384f | 384-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-384s | 384-bit | Small |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-512f | 512-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SHAKE-512s | 512-bit | Small |

### SM3-based Instances

| Instance | Security Level | Variant |
|----------|---------------|---------|
| Phoenix-SM3-128f | 128-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SM3-128s | 128-bit | Small |
| Phoenix-SM3-192f | 192-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SM3-192s | 192-bit | Small |
| Phoenix-SM3-256f | 256-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SM3-256s | 256-bit | Small |
| Phoenix-SM3-384f | 384-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SM3-384s | 384-bit | Small |
| Phoenix-SM3-512f | 512-bit | Fast |
| Phoenix-SM3-512s | 512-bit | Small |

## Building

To build and generate KAT vectors for any instance:

```sh
cd Implementations/Reference_Implementation/Phoenix-SHAKE-128s
make kat
```

The generated KAT vector file will be written to `output/KAT_SIG_Phoenix-SHAKE-128s.txt`.

